{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-11-7","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：平面与平行线与线段","englishTitle":"If two straight lines be parallel and points be taken at random on each of them, the straight line joining the points is in the same plane with the parallel straight lines.","book":11,"number":7,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.7","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.7/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":7,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-11-7@raw-abdd0d791f9b3c1b","contentId":"euclid-11-7","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"abdd0d791f9b3c1b72296471232bea74c43b9115b50dcdf2f196b409e87db16b","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-11-7.statement","euclid-11-7.construction.1","euclid-11-7.proof.1","euclid-11-7.construction.2","euclid-11-7.proof.2","euclid-11-7.conclusion","euclid-11-7.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-11-7.statement","contentId":"euclid-11-7","revisionId":"euclid-11-7@raw-abdd0d791f9b3c1b","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"5256dd80173cefd9aac5f7b9fa0d65ead74e7f9bc5a6a46c0ba2d54d1c693834","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If two straight lines be parallel and points be taken at random on each of them, the straight line joining the points is in the same plane with the parallel straight lines."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果两条直线平行,每一条直线随机取出点数,连接点的直线是同一条平面线和平行直线。"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-7.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-11-7","revisionId":"euclid-11-7@raw-abdd0d791f9b3c1b","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"bcecd75f6869f2e3b4ebe795ce3d479b2dc5a69047110f9cfd44cd25453341fa","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let AB, CD be two parallel straight lines, and let points E, F be taken at random on them respectively; I say that the straight line joining the points E, F is in the same plane with the parallel straight lines."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让AB,CD线成为两个平行的直线,让E,F点分别随机地标上;我说连接E,F点的直线与平行直线位于平面上。"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-7.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-11-7","revisionId":"euclid-11-7@raw-abdd0d791f9b3c1b","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"72ac971602099dbb8f1a8c8f5d364204c471bd90fc3d8232d6ca41a0191cefdd","citations":["euclid-11-3"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For suppose it is not, but, if possible, let it be in a more elevated plane as EGF, and let a plane be drawn through EGF; it will then make, as section in the plane of reference, a straight line. [[XI. 3](/principles/euclid-11-3)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"假设不是,但如果可能,则以平面升为EGF,平面升为EGF;然后,平面升为EGF;然后,它将像参考文献平面的一节那样,成为一条直线。 [[XI. 3](/principles/euclid-11-3)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-7.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-11-7","revisionId":"euclid-11-7@raw-abdd0d791f9b3c1b","order":3,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c92fabef1549d8d7b0fdd0aba7700c0fd3e5cc9cfb9600e8c3f3ba8f7814d2f6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let it make it, as EF; therefore the two straight lines EGF, EF will enclose an area: which is impossible."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让它成为EF,因此,两条直线EGF、EF将加盖一个区域:这是不可能的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-7.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-11-7","revisionId":"euclid-11-7@raw-abdd0d791f9b3c1b","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8b39f195162878f91e21ba62637e5cd1d424c2a257648fd0a1d16fd2a44db24f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the straight line joined from E to F is not in a plane more elevated; therefore the straight line joined from E to F is in the plane through the parallel straight lines AB, CD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,连接E至F的直线没有在平面高线中;因此,连接E至F的直线在平面高线中,而平行直线为AB、CD。"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-7.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-11-7","revisionId":"euclid-11-7@raw-abdd0d791f9b3c1b","order":5,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d41f4fe56dd428c759377c807a93013dffbbe29c7596acfdac57dd182cad51b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,等等,证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-7.source","contentId":"euclid-11-7","revisionId":"euclid-11-7@raw-abdd0d791f9b3c1b","order":6,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c4f2e940b17782cbf53ff83d828b88d6e310bbf8d31eb621ba05dc2be58a22cd","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.7/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.7\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-11-7:euclid-11-3:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-11-7","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-11-7.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-11-3","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.7","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.7/","sourceLabel":"XI. 3"}}],"incomingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-11-8:euclid-11-7:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-11-8","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-11-8.construction.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-11-7","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.8","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.8/","sourceLabel":"XI. 7"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-12-17:euclid-11-7:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-12-17","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-12-17.proof.10"],"targetContentId":"euclid-11-7","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.17","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.17/","sourceLabel":"XI. 7"}}],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-11-7:euclid-11-3:explicit","id":"euclid-11-3","book":11,"number":3,"kind":"proposition","title":"两个相交平面的交线是一条直线","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"dependents":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-11-8:euclid-11-7:explicit","id":"euclid-11-8","book":11,"number":8,"kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：平面与平行线与角","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"},{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-12-17:euclid-11-7:explicit","id":"euclid-12-17","book":12,"number":17,"kind":"proposition","t